  - The whole room-box header (color dot + name + count) is now the button that opens the room color/brightness palette; removed the small separate color circle. The vertical on/off toggle still stops propagation so it doesn't open the palette.
  - The per-room scene chip row was removed. Inside the room's LightEditor there's now a pretty gradient "✦ Scenes" button (passed via a new optional `children` slot on LightEditor, so individual-light editors don't show it). Clicking it closes the palette and opens a modal.
  - New SceneModal lists every global scene as a gradient tile (click to apply to this room) plus a "Save this room's look as a scene" footer. Lights remain independently editable.
